.Dd October 14, 2026
.Dt MSMAN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm msman
.Nd archive files into a date-based directory tree
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl a Ar file
.Op Fl l
.Op Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility copies files into an archive directory, organised by the date on
which they were archived.
.Pp
The archive is the directory named
.Pa archive
in the current working directory.
It must already exist;
.Nm
will not create it.
.Pp
Within the archive, each file is stored under a subdirectory of the form
.Pa YYYY/MM/DD ,
based on the current local date.
Intermediate directories are created as needed.
For example, a file named
.Pa notes.txt
archived on 14 October 2026 is stored as
.Pa archive/2026/10/14/notes.txt .
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a Ar file
Archive
.Ar file .
The file is copied, not moved, so the original is left in place.
Only regular files are accepted.
If a file of the same name already exists in that day's directory, the
user is prompted before it is overwritten.
.It Fl l
List all archived files, one path per line, in sorted order.
.It Fl h
Print a usage message to standard error.
.El
.Pp
Options are processed in the order given, so
.Fl a
and
.Fl l
may be combined in one invocation.
If run without arguments,
.Nm
prints a usage message and exits.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa archive/
Archive directory, relative to the current working directory.
.It Pa archive/YYYY/MM/DD/
Directory holding the files archived on the given date.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Specifically:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
The archive directory is missing, the file to archive does not exist or is
not a regular file, a directory or file could not be created, or no
arguments were given.
.It 2
An unknown option or an unexpected argument was given.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create the archive directory:
.Pp
.Dl $ mkdir archive
.Pp
Archive a file:
.Pp
.Dl $ msman -a report.pdf
.Pp
List archived files:
.Pp
.Dl $ msman -l
.Pp
Archive a file, then list the archive:
.Pp
.Dl $ msman -a report.pdf -l
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It msman: missing directory: archive/
The archive directory does not exist in the current working directory.
.It msman: Ns Ar file Ns : No such file
.Ar file
does not exist or is not a regular file.
.It msman: unexpected argument: Ar arg
Non-option arguments were supplied.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cp 1 ,
.Xr find 1 ,
.Xr getopts 1
.Sh CAVEATS
The archive location is fixed and relative to the current directory, so
.Nm
should always be run from the directory that contains
.Pa archive/ .
